In YDSE, let intensities of two identical coherent sources $S_1 and S_2$ is $I_0$. Then, resultant intensity, I=2 I_0 \cos ^2 $\frac{\phi}{2}$ where, $\phi=$ phase difference.
When path difference is $\lambda$, then \phi_1=$\frac{2 \pi}{\lambda} \text{ (path difference)$ and $} \phi_1=\frac{2 \pi}{\lambda} \lambda=2 \pi$ When path difference is $\frac{\lambda}{4}$, then $\begin{aligned}
\phi_2 & =\frac{2 \pi}{\lambda} \frac{\lambda}{4}=\frac{\pi}{2}\\
\therefore \quad \frac{I_1}{I_2}& =\frac{2 I_0 \cos ^2 \frac{\phi_1}{2}}{2 I_0 \cos ^2 \frac{\phi_2}{2}}=\frac{\cos ^2\left(\frac{2 \pi}{2}\right)}{\cos ^2\left(\frac{\pi}{4}\right)}=\frac{\cos ^2(\pi)}{\cos ^2 \frac{\pi}{4}}\\
& =\frac{1}{(1 / 2)}=\frac{2}{1}
\end{aligned}$ Hence, $I_1: I_2=2: 1$

